sieve-filter-v1
; A fractal's ruleset (sieve-fractal-v1 or v2, SPECIFICATIONS 12.0t, core/include/sieve/fractal.hpp) written
; as a filter: v1's rulesets as format-fractal-v1 passes them, and v2's, the L-systems v1 cannot write:
; "sieve-fractal-v2", then "lsystem ANGLE" with an angle that has a tenth (0.1 to 359.9, as 22.5), or
; "lsystem ANGLE scale RATIO" (any angle; RATIO 0.001 to 0.999, no 0 at its end) with " and ' among the
; symbols (the step RATIO times as long, or as short), then "axiom WORD" and one or more "rule SYMBOL
; WORD" as v1's. As format-fractal-v1, the rules' order by symbol is the reader's alone, so its
; survivors are the reader's rulesets with their rules in any order; tools/check_formats.py checks
; every other verdict.
; Written by tools/grammars.py (the grammar is there; this table is what it compiles to).

id        format-fractal
version   2
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   ascii96
describe  One sieve-fractal-v1 or sieve-fractal-v2 ruleset (its rules' order aside): the fractal dimension's line, each ruleset at its address in fractal-space-v2 (IDEAS 19.235, list X2).

class     c0    @0                       ; \n
class     c1    @1                       ;  
class     c2    @3 @8                    ; "'
class     c3    @12 @60 @62 @93          ; +[]|
class     c4    @14                      ; -
class     c5    @15                      ; .
class     c6    @17                      ; 0
class     c7    @18                      ; 1
class     c8    @19                      ; 2
class     c9    @20                      ; 3
class     c10   @21..@22                 ; 45
class     c11   @23..@26                 ; 6789
class     c12   @34..@59                 ; ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ
class     c13   @66                      ; a
class     c14   @67                      ; b
class     c15   @68                      ; c
class     c16   @69 @72..@73 @75..@76 @81..@82 @88 @91 ; dghjkpqwz
class     c17   @70                      ; e
class     c18   @71                      ; f
class     c19   @74                      ; i
class     c20   @77                      ; l
class     c21   @78                      ; m
class     c22   @79                      ; n
class     c23   @80                      ; o
class     c24   @83                      ; r
class     c25   @84                      ; s
class     c26   @85                      ; t
class     c27   @86                      ; u
class     c28   @87                      ; v
class     c29   @89                      ; x
class     c30   @90                      ; y

